        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Guide Gemini users to Antigravity on consumer-tier shutdown",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Detect Google's `UNSUPPORTED_CLIENT` / `IneligibleTierError` migration responses in Gemini quota, `loadCodeAssist`, and token-refresh paths.\n- Surface a dedicated `consumerTierDeprecated` error that points individual / AI Pro / Ultra users toward CodexBar's Antigravity provider instead of generic auth failures.\n- Add migration guidance at Gemini login (Terminal launch), in `notLoggedIn` / Antigravity `notRunning` errors, and via a Settings action to enable Antigravity when the migration signal is detected.\n- Document the June 2026 consumer-tier migration behavior in `docs/gemini.md` and `docs/antigravity.md`.\n\nThis PR handles surfaced Google deprecation responses and migration guidance. It does not restore Gemini provider quota for blocked consumer tiers, auto-fallback to Antigravity, or capture Terminal `gemini` OAuth stdout/stderr directly; those failures are only surfaced when CodexBar can observe them through the status/API probe paths or the added login/setup copy.\n\nFixes #1929\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `swift test --filter GeminiConsumerTierMigration`\n- [x] `swift test --filter GeminiStatusProbeAPITests`\n- [x] `make check`\n- [ ] Manual: enable Gemini on a consumer-tier account blocked by Google and confirm the menu/CLI shows the Antigravity migration message\n\n### Manual verification note\nI did not run the full live OAuth flow because it requires using a real consumer Google account and clearing/re-authorizing local Gemini credentials. Locally, the existing Gemini credential is expired and returns `401 UNAUTHENTICATED`, so I could not capture a live `UNSUPPORTED_CLIENT` response. The implemented behavior is covered by stubbed responses for the API/status-probe paths. This PR intentionally handles surfaced Google deprecation responses and adds migration guidance, without claiming live OAuth verification.",
